                                "text": "Hackenbeck’s analysis relies on the adage, “we are what we eat and drink,” she said. Different diets will leave characteristic signatures in the carbon, nitrogen and strontium isotopes contained inside a person’s bones (elements come in different versions, or isotopes, that differ in mass)."
